    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint is an OfficeFloor function pipeline. On successful create it already saves the owner (assigning its id) and audits the event; I added a welcome-notification step after that.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`: emits one line via the `NOTIFY` logger carrying the new owner's id and `memberId`, mirroring the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` style.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `respond`, so it runs after `SaveOwner` (id assigned) and after `DeduplicateMemberId` (member id finalized), under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline.\n\n## Verification\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line containing both the owner id and memberId:\n\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification queued for owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
